  "question": {
    "text": "If the&nbsp;system of linear equations,<br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math><br />has more than two solutions, then <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, is equal to."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>,<br />If <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />If <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math>,&nbsp;must pass through <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2,4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4,0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p><math><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math><br />And <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><math><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p>"
  }
}